## Ops checklist \'97 step by step\
\
Do these in order. Web Google first, native last.\
\
### 1. Google Cloud OAuth client\
\
1. Open [Google Cloud Console](https://console.cloud.google.com/) 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  your project (or create one)\
2. **APIs & Services 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  OAuth consent screen** \'97 External, fill app name / support email / logo if you have it\
3. **APIs & Services 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  Credentials 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  Create credentials 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  OAuth client ID**\
   - Application type: **Web application**\
   - Authorized JavaScript origins: `https://voiceora.io` (and `http://localhost:3000` for local)\
   - Authorized redirect URIs:  \
     `https://<YOUR-SUPABASE-PROJECT-REF>.supabase.co/auth/v1/callback`\
4. Copy the **Client ID** and **Client secret**\
\
### 2. Supabase 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  enable Google\
\
1. Supabase Dashboard 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  your project 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  **Authentication 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  Providers 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  Google**\
2. Toggle **Enabled**\
3. Paste Client ID + Client secret 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  Save\
4. **Authentication 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  URL Configuration 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  Redirect URLs** \'97 add (if missing):\
   - `https://voiceora.io/auth/callback`\
   - `http://localhost:3000/auth/callback`\
   - (native, later) `com.voiceora.io://auth/callback`\
\
### 3. Vercel 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  turn the button on\
\
1. Vercel 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  Voiceora project 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  **Settings 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  Environment Variables**\
2. Add / set `NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_AUTH_ENABLED` = `true`\
   - Start with **Preview** if you want to test first; then **Production** when ready\
3. Redeploy (or wait for next deploy) so the client sees the env var\
4. On `/sign-in` and `/sign-up` (desktop browser), confirm the Google button appears and completes sign-in\
\
### 4. Supabase 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  Confirm signup email template\
\
1. Supabase 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  **Authentication 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  Email Templates 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  Confirm signup**\
2. Keep the confirmation link **and** add the code. Example body:\
\
```html\
<h2>Confirm your signup</h2>\
<p>Your code: <strong>\{\{ .Token \}\}</strong></p>\
<p>Or click: <a href="\{\{ .ConfirmationURL \}\}">Confirm your email</a></p>\
```\
\
3. Save\
4. Test: sign up with a real inbox 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  you should get a **6-digit code** (UI) **and** a working link (fallback)\
5. Confirm SMTP for `support@voiceora.io` actually delivers before taking the holding page down\
\
### 5. Native deep link (only after web Google works)\
\
1. Supabase 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  **Redirect URLs** 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  add exactly:  \
   `com.voiceora.io://auth/callback`  \
   (no `?next=\'85` \'97 code already uses the bare URL)\
2. Locally on `main`:\
\
```bash\
npx cap sync ios\
cd ios/App && pod install && cd ../..\
```\
\
3. Open the iOS project in Xcode, run on a device/simulator\
4. Confirm `Info.plist` has `CFBundleURLTypes` / scheme `com.voiceora.io` (already committed)\
5. Temporarily remove the two native guards to test:\
   - `components/auth/auth-form.tsx` \'97 the `&& !isNativePlatform()` on Google visibility\
   - `components/auth/google-sign-in-button.tsx` \'97 the early `if (isNativePlatform()) return null`\
6. Run Google sign-in in the app 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  Safari/Browser sheet 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  deep link back 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  land signed in\
7. If that works, commit the guard removal on a new branch and open a small PR  \
   If it fails, leave the guards in place (web Google still works)\
\
---\
\
**Suggested order for launch day:** 1 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  2 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  3 (web Google) 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  4 (OTP emails) 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  public launch 
\f2 \uc0\u8594 
\f1  5 (native) when you have Xcode time.}